        "text": "Page: Lótus Bridge. Sentence: Lotus Bridge () is a cross-border bridge linking the Cotai reclamation area of Macau with Hengqin Island in Zhuhai, Guangdong Province, People's Republic of China (PRC).\nPage: Lótus Bridge. Sentence: The bridge is the road crossing between mainland China and Macau.\nPage: Hengqin. Sentence: Hengqin, sometimes known as Ilha de Montanha in Portuguese\",\" is an island in Zhuhai, a prefecture-level city and Special Economic Zone in the Guangdong province of the People's Republic of China.\nPage: Hengqin. Sentence: Parts of Hengqin are leased to Macau by the State Council of the People's Republic of China in 2009.\nPage: Chimelong International Ocean Resort. Sentence: The resort is located at Hengqin, Zhuhai, China.\nPage: Hoi Fan. Sentence: Clube de Natação Hoi Fan (Traditional Chinese: 海帆, literally meaning sail of the sea) is a Macau football club, which plays in the town of Macau.",
